# Vulkan submission translates the shared vertex ABI; geometry stays in ui/.
import types.dl
import svg.dl

to get the native UI [surface] in {a pointer to UI view:view}:
    return view's window as a pointer to native UI surface

to set native UI clipping in {a pointer to UI view:view}:
    set surface to the native UI surface in view
    set first to UI surface point (a UI point at (view's clip's x) and (view's clip's y)) in view
    set last to UI surface point (a UI point at (view's clip's x + view's clip's width) and (view's clip's y + view's clip's height)) in view
    set rectangle to a new VkRect2D
    set scale to view's pixel scale
    set left to the maximum of 0 and ((the floor of (first's x * scale)) as an integer)
    set top to the maximum of 0 and ((the floor of (first's y * scale)) as an integer)
    set right to the minimum of (the framebuffer width of (surface's resource)) and ((the ceiling of (last's x * scale)) as an integer)
    set bottom to the minimum of (the framebuffer height of (surface's resource)) and ((the ceiling of (last's y * scale)) as an integer)
    set rectangle's offset' x to left
    set rectangle's offset' y to top
    set rectangle's extent' width to (the maximum of 0 and (right - left)) as a 32 bit unsigned integer
    set rectangle's extent' height to (the maximum of 0 and (bottom - top)) as a 32 bit unsigned integer
    set the clipping rectangle of (surface's frame) to rectangle

to begin native UI {a pointer to UI view:view}:
    set surface to the native UI surface in view
    set state to surface's resource as a pointer to DynlexGraphics
    set ink to view's theme's background
    set surface's frame to a new graphics frame in (surface's resource) with background red ((graphics color channel (ink's red) for state) as a floating-point number), green ((graphics color channel (ink's green) for state) as a floating-point number), blue ((graphics color channel (ink's blue) for state) as a floating-point number) and alpha 1.0
    set view's drawable to surface's frame's drawable
    if view's drawable = false:
        if ((the framebuffer width of (surface's resource)) > 0) and ((the framebuffer height of (surface's resource)) > 0):
            animate UI view view
    if view's drawable:
        set state's model to an identity graphics matrix
        set state's camera to an identity graphics matrix
        set state's projection to a graphics orthographic projection from left 0.0 right (view's width as a floating-point number) top 0.0 bottom (view's height as a floating-point number) near -1.0 far 1.0
    set view's linear colors to the graphics surface uses sRGB in state

to present native UI {a pointer to UI view:view}:
    set surface to the native UI surface in view
    display surface's frame

to submit native UI {a pointer to UI view:view} vertices {a pointer to UI vertex:vertices} counting {integer:count} with {a pointer:texture}:
    if (view's clip's width <= 0.0) or (view's clip's height <= 0.0):
        return nothing
    set surface to the native UI surface in view
    set state to surface's resource as a pointer to DynlexGraphics
    set native UI clipping in view
    begin a graphics triangle stream with texture (texture as a pointer to DynlexGraphicsTexture) in state
    set index to 0
    loop while index < count:
        set vertex to the item at index in vertices
        store vertex's u into state's current_vertex's texture_coordinates at 0
        store vertex's v into state's current_vertex's texture_coordinates at 1
        store vertex's red into state's current_vertex's color at 0
        store vertex's green into state's current_vertex's color at 1
        store vertex's blue into state's current_vertex's color at 2
        store vertex's alpha into state's current_vertex's color at 3
        append a graphics vertex at x (vertex's x as a floating-point number) y (vertex's y as a floating-point number) z 0.0 in state
        increment index
    finish the graphics triangle stream in state

to get the native UI icon in {a pointer to UI view:view} from {a pointer to UI SVG icon:icon} sized {integer:size}:
    set surface to the native UI surface in view
    set pixels to the coverage of SVG (the value at icon) at pixel size size using (surface's library)
    return (a graphics texture resource from (the data of pixels) with width size height size channels (1 as a 32 bit unsigned integer) in (surface's resource as a pointer to DynlexGraphics)) as a pointer

to release native UI texture in {a pointer to UI view:view} holding {a pointer:texture}:
    release graphics texture resource (texture as a pointer to DynlexGraphicsTexture)
